# Pull request body

When creating or updating a GitHub pull request with `gh pr create` / `gh pr edit`:

1. Read `.github/pull_request_template.md`.
2. Fill **that** template as the PR body. Do not invent a different structure (no custom `## Summary` / `## Test plan` layout).
3. Always fill **Testing**, **Risk**, and **How to revert** with concrete content for this change (not placeholders). Agents may draft them; the author still owns the sign-off.
4. Delete optional sections that do not apply (e.g. Screenshots when there is no UI change).
5. Keep the Description concrete; use the Ready checklist only for items that matter for this PR.
